  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the App\'s Structure**\n\nI\'m now diving deep into the user\'s prompt, scrutinizing the instructions for the app\'s structure and the visual style they\'ve specified. I\'m paying close attention to the requested \"look\" of the screens and noting any mention of hotlinking images and the referenced HTML. I need to fully understand their vision before proceeding.\n\n\n**Defining the Design System**\n\nI\'ve just gotten a major boost! I\'ve uncovered the complete design system specifications, including color palettes, for \"Obsidian Kinetic\". I\'m now integrating this vital information into the visual design plan, ensuring every aspect aligns with the provided details. I\'m focusing on incorporating these color values into the framework of the app\'s components, making sure everything is consistent.\n\n\n**Incorporating Key Style Elements**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided color palette, \"Obsidian Kinetic\", with the overarching \"Dark Minimalist Editorial and Technical Glassmorphism\" style. I\'m focusing on blending the base colors, dark surfaces, structural lines, and neon accents to ensure a cohesive and impactful visual experience. The console input styling and brand narrative helps create a precise and competent presentation.\n\n\n**Reviewing Screen Components**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the components outlined in the markdown, particularly the top bar, hero section, and screen showcases. I\'m focusing on their interactive elements and the specified visual characteristics. I\'m looking into how these will be implemented with brand title and action buttons. I\'m taking note of the space grotesque typography and technical badges in the hero section.\n\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Demonstrations**\n\nI\'m now focusing on interactive elements, specifically around the performance tests. I\'m building out a system for users to test 60 FPS Skia animations, benchmark rendering times, toggle JSI bridge versus legacy bridge simulation, and adjust thread concurrency. I am also developing ways to view live frame budget graphs. I\'m focusing on the performance and the user experience.\n\n\n**Constructing Inspector Interfaces**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing three specific inspector components. I\'m focusing on the first, the \"Code & Architecture Explorer,\" which will feature a code block panel with color-coded syntax and interactive tabs for different files. The second, an \"Architecture Comparison Tool,\" provides a visualizer of the Legacy Bridge versus the New Architecture, highlighting their differences. The final component I\'m building is the \"Commit & Architecture Telemetry Log\" to show performance gain metrics with horizontal rows for easy readability.\n\n\n**Designing Console Interaction**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the interactive cockpit terminal console and implementing the specified features. I\'m building out commands like `help`, `skills`, `projects`, `benchmark`, `audit`, and `contact`, ensuring each provides a dynamic and informative response. The console must feature command history, tab completion, and instant execution, providing a smooth user experience.\n\n\n"
