  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the User Prompt**\n\nOkay, I\'m now drilling down into the specifics of the user\'s request. I\'m taking a fresh look at the attachment, specifically the markdown file, and re-evaluating the user\'s prompt to ensure I have a comprehensive grasp of what\'s expected. My primary focus is understanding how these pieces fit together to determine what kind of app I should build.\n\n\n**Reviewing the Design System**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the markdown file, specifically the \"Obsidian Kinetic\" design system. The explicit instructions dictate I should only generate images if the user explicitly asks. The design system is defined, its theme being avant-garde editorial with a developer cockpit focus for React Native architecture, which provides significant clarity on how to proceed.\n\n\n**Defining the UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of the UI components outlined in the design system. I\'ve fully documented the color palette, typography selections, and grid structure, with each one fully implemented, and I\'m developing detailed specs. I have begun drafting the Top Navigation Bar and Hero Section specifications based on the markdown file.\n\n\n**Designing the Preview Stage**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the interactive mobile preview stage, aiming for a rich user experience. I\'m prioritizing the \"Aetheria Trading Terminal\" screen, which is designed to feature a real-time orderbook and candlestick graph rendering. My objective is to achieve a smooth 60 FPS performance using SVG/Canvas with live price ticks. I\'m also planning to incorporate a depth chart for rapid order placement, ensuring a fully interactive experience.\n\n\n**Developing the Showcase Features**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the features. I\'m prioritizing the integration of JSI thread telemetry, which will be coupled with BioPulse telemetry for real-time biometric wave visualization. I also plan to implement the Vortex 3D/Shader Engine for an interactive physics demo and Chronos for local SQLite mutation visualization. I\'m working on the device controls, including frame rate and architecture toggles to demonstrate performance differences between legacy and JSI modes.\n\n\n**Expanding the Project Scope**\n\nI\'m now integrating detailed case studies. I\'ve drafted four high-tier technical studies, including architecture diagrams, benchmarks, and technical dossiers. These focus on Aetheria Mobile, Synapse Health, Vortex Motion, and Chronos Ledger. Furthermore, I\'m working to add expandable architecture deep-dives for each study, and I\'m developing an interactive code and systems architecture inspector.\n\n\n**Refining the Terminal Interface**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the Mac terminal window design for the demo. I\'m focusing on the implementation of a high-contrast syntax highlighting scheme, the introduction of interactive explanation tooltips for complicated code lines, and the addition of copy buttons. I\'ve also detailed an interactive Architecture Blueprint visualizer, providing a clear flow diagram of the React UI Layer, JSI Interface, C++ Native Core, and the GPU.\n\n**Finalizing the Telemetry Log**\n\nI\'m now making refinements to the commit and architecture telemetry log. I\'m working to create a real-time filtered log of engineering milestones. I have integrated monospaced timestamps, headlines in Space Grotesk, and display performance gains with color-coded positive and negative results. Filters are also being incorporated to categorize the data.\n\n\n"
