  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Application Components**\n\nI\'m currently breaking down the application components based on the requirements outlined in `Image_3_37305245.markdown`. I\'m starting with the header and top bar, looking at the 3-zone contract: brand title, and am getting ready to move on.\n\n\n**Defining Visual Structure**\n\nI\'ve moved on to defining the visual structure, particularly the hero section. I\'m focusing on the status indicator, headline, body description, and quick action buttons. Specifically, I\'m fleshing out the appearance of the \"LAUNCH MOBILE STAGE\" button to enhance its impact. The color and pulsing animation of the indicator chip are getting detailed consideration. I\'m looking at the terminal button next!\n\n\n**Evaluating Performance Metrics**\n\nI\'m now examining performance metrics for the \'SI CORE\'. I\'m paying close attention to the Adjacency Proof Metrics Strip, specifically the `120 FPS` achieved through Native Skia & Fabric Pipeline, the `< 2.4ms` Zero-Copy JSI HostObject Dispatch, and the impressive `0.00%` Bridge Serialization Dropped Frames, as well as the `99.98%` Crash-Free Sessions. I\'m taking notes on these numbers, to see how to incorporate them.\n\n**Building Interactive Simulator**\n\nI\'m now building the interactive mobile stage, a live device simulator. I\'m focusing on the simulated mobile screen frame, aiming for an 8px radius and a bezel tinted with `#1A2234`. I\'ll present live embedded micro-interactions and optimized video captures, complete with a dynamic status bar. I\'m also going to create a screen switcher for 4 interactive mobile prototypes.\n\n\n**Developing Interactive Prototype**\n\nI am working on an interactive mobile stage prototype, focusing on several key interactions. I\'m showcasing instant JSI execution with a tick latency under 1.8ms. Additionally, I am displaying live animated ECG/PPG cardiac waveforms, and BLE packet stream visualizer. The kinetic physics interactions, like drag and spring, will be shown with real-time worklet calculations. I\'m also including an offline-first CRDT ledger with simulated network states.\n\n\n**Contrasting Bridge Architectures**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a direct comparison between the legacy bridge and the JSI architecture. The FPS drops and frame time spikes I\'m observing with the legacy bridge, along with JSON serialization warnings, are quite stark. I\'m noting the contrast when switching back to JSI, where performance is immediately restored. I will incorporate this device mode data. I\'m also including the frame budget inspector, showing real-time JS Thread, UI Thread, and GPU Render times.\n\n\n**Incorporating Performance Data**\n\nI\'m now integrating performance data to demonstrate efficiency gains. I\'m focusing on the significant memory footprint reduction, the FPS increase in lists, and the cold start time reduction. The tech stack components will need to be highlighted. I\'m thinking of creating a modal that presents an architectural dossier, accessed via an \"Inspect Architecture & Code\" button, which leads to the next thoughts. Then, I\'m thinking of creating a display panel, with various components.\n\n\n**Designing Telemetry Log**\n\nI\'m now designing the commit and architecture telemetry log, focusing on a clean, horizontal row format. I\'m partitioning rows with a 1px solid border, and including filter chips for various aspects like JSI & C++, Fabric, and Hermes GC. The log will feature monospaced timestamps, feature headlines with descriptions, and performance gains highlighted in a specific color. I\'m also planning an interactive cockpit terminal console, which supports commands for various functions.\n\n\n**Planning Audit Interaction**\n\nI\'m now planning the \"Interactive Architecture Audit Request\" modal. I\'m focusing on its high-contrast, glassmorphic design and the specific details clients can provide: app type, architecture targets, and contact info. The instant confirmation simulation upon submission will also need a bit of work. Finally, I\'ve checked the existing packages to make sure we have everything we need, and it seems like we do. I\'m going to start organizing the code into modular components.\n\n\n**Organizing Code Components**\n\nI\'m now diving into the code, starting with the TypeScript interfaces I\'ll need for various data models: `Projects`, `Telemetry Logs`, `Code Files`, `Simulator Apps`, `Benchmarks`, and `Audit Requests`. I\'ve also found the data models, such as portfolio data and a three-zone top bar contract. I have started examining the components.\n\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
      id: "call_1673084634527967727"
      name: "write_to_file"
      arguments_json: "{\"Append\":false, \"CodeContent\":\"export interface Project {\\n  id: string;\\n  title: string;\\n  subtitle: string;\\n  category: string;\\n  year: string;\\n  summary: string;\\n  architectureHighlight: string;\\n  clientType: string;\\n  metrics: {\\n    label: string;\\n    value: string;\\n    delta: string;\\n  }[];\\n  techStack: string[];\\n  keyChallenges: string[];\\n  architecturalDecisions: {\\n    decision: string;\\n    rationale: string;\\n    outcome: string;\\n  }[];\\n  codeSnippetPreview?: {\\n    filename: string;\\n    language: string;\\n    code: string;\\n  };\\n}\\n\\nexport interface TelemetryItem {\\n  id: string;\\n  timestamp: string;\\n  headline: string;\\n  subsystem: \'JSI & C++\' | \'Fabric & Rendering\' | \'Hermes GC\' | \'Turbomodules\' | \'Storage/CRDT\';\\n  metric: string;\\n  details: string;\\n  commitHash: string;\\n}\\n\\nexport interface CodeFile {\\n  id: string;\\n  filename: string;\\n  language: string;\\n  description: string;\\n  code: string;\\n  keyInsights: {\\n    lineRange: string;\\n    title: string;\\n    explanation: string;\\n  }[];\\n}\\n\\nexport type SimulatorAppId = \'trading\' | \'biopulse\' | \'physics\' | \'crdt\';\\n\\nexport interface AuditFormData {\\n  name: string;\\n  email: string;\\n  company: string;\\n  scope: string;\\n  currentBottlenecks: string;\\n  targetTimeline: string;\\n}\\n\", \"Description\":\"Define core TypeScript data models for projects, telemetry items, code inspector, and simulator apps\", \"Overwrite\":true, \"TargetFile\":\"/src/types/index.ts\", \"toolAction\":\"Creating types file\", \"toolSummary\":\"Write TypeScript types in src/types/index.ts\"}"
