    response: "I have built the **Obsidian Kinetic** mobile systems architecture and portfolio cockpit adhering strictly to your design specification.\n\n### Highlights & Implemented Features\n\n1. **Brand Aesthetic & Design System (Obsidian Kinetic)**\n   - **Palette**: Grounded on Dark Void (`#080B12`), with modular glass panels (`#111827`, `#1A2234`), structural Cartesian subgrid lines (`#273244`), and kinetic bioluminescent accents in Lime Neon (`#9FE870`), Cyan Neon (`#65D6C5`), Amber (`#FFB86C`), and Crimson (`#FF5555`).\n   - **Typography**: Paired **Space Grotesk** for display and headlines, **Inter** for narrative copy, and **JetBrains Mono** with tabular numerals for runtime telemetry and code.\n   - **Top Bar Contract**: Follows the 3-zone standard (single-element brand wordmark, clean single-line navigation links, and primary kinetic `Request Audit` CTA).\n\n2. **Interactive Mobile Preview Stage (Live Device Simulator)**\n   - **Aetheria HFT Terminal**: Live simulated WebSocket orderbook depth, real-time price ticks, and instant buy/sell trade execution feedback.\n   - **BioPulse Continuous Telemetry**: Real-time continuous 120Hz Lead II ECG waveform, cardiac vitals (BPM, SpO2, HRV), and raw BLE packet hex streaming.\n   - **Vortex Gesture Physics**: Interactive draggable touch canvas powered by UI-thread spring calculations, displaying live coordinates and worklet latency.\n   - **Chronos Offline CRDT Ledger**: Interactive Online/Airplane mode toggle with direct SQLite C++ JSI commit simulation and vector clock conflict resolution.\n   - **Architecture Mode Comparator**: Live toggle between **New Architecture JSI (Zero-Copy C++)** and **Legacy Bridge (JSON-over-String)**, demonstrating frame rate degradation (dropping to ~36 FPS with Hermes GC pressure) vs. locked 120 FPS.\n\n3. **Systems & JSI Code Inspector**\n   - Terminal window styling with window dots, line numbers, and custom token highlighting.\n   - Interactive files: `AetheriaOrderBookHost.cpp`, `BioPulseShadowNode.mm`, `VortexFragmentShader.tsx`, and `ChronosVectorEngine.ts`.\n   - Click-to-inspect architectural invariants explaining zero-copy buffers, Yoga layout bypass, and Metal/Vulkan shader pipelines.\n   - Visual architectural pipeline mapping the thread distribution from the JS Thread (Hermes) through JSI C++ pointers into the Metal/Vulkan GPU surface.\n\n4. **Empirical Benchmarks & Dynamic Stress Tester**\n   - Interactive slider adjusting simulated WebSocket throughput (500 to 5,000 ticks/sec), dynamically calculating serialization lag, memory churn, and frame budget status.\n\n5. **Architecture Telemetry Log**\n   - Clean horizontal rows partitioned by structural hairlines with monospaced timestamps, Space Grotesk feature headlines, commit hashes, and `#65D6C5` performance gains (`+58 FPS`, `-32% TTI`, `-28MB Heap`). Filterable by subsystem.\n\n6. **Interactive Cockpit Terminal Console (`> adarsh.tech ~ $`)**\n   - Accessible via the top bar or by pressing the backtick/tilde key (`` ` ``).\n   - Executable commands: `neofetch`, `help`, `skills`, `projects`, `benchmarks`, `cat bio.md`, `audit`, and `clear`, with command history navigation.\n\n7. **Detailed Architecture Dossiers & Audit Request Flow**\n   - In-depth modal dossiers for case studies detailing challenges, architectural decisions, and outcomes.\n   - Systems review scheduling form generating verifiable reference IDs upon submission."
    thinking: "**Revisiting Design Components**\n\nI\'m currently meticulously reviewing the Obsidian Kinetic design system, as documented in `/public/assets/aistudio/Image_3_37305245.markdown`. I\'m starting with the foundational elements: the dark void, and the secondary and tertiary surfaces, ensuring their consistent application and exploring any potential conflicts or gaps in the specifications. My aim is a complete and accurate picture.\n\n\n**Analyzing System Specifications**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down into the system\'s structural elements, focusing on the lime neon, cyan neon, code amber, and error crimson color palette, and their role in the design. I\'m actively verifying the font choices (Space Grotesk, Inter, JetBrains Mono) are correctly integrated. Furthermore, I\'ve started examining the UI\'s practical aspects, such as the top bar contract, the LED status indicator, and the mobile preview stage micro-interactions.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have built the **Obsidian Kinetic** mobile systems architecture and portfolio cockpit adhering strictly to your design specification.\n\n### Highlights & Implemented Features\n\n1. **Brand Aesthetic & Design System (Obsidian Kinetic)**\n   - **Palette**: Grounded on Dark Void (`#080B12`), with modular glass panels (`#111827`, `#1A2234`), structural Cartesian subgrid lines (`#273244`), and kinetic bioluminescent accents in Lime Neon (`#9FE870`), Cyan Neon (`#65D6C5`), Amber (`#FFB86C`), and Crimson (`#FF5555`).\n   - **Typography**: Paired **Space Grotesk** for display and headlines, **Inter** for narrative copy, and **JetBrains Mono** with tabular numerals for runtime telemetry and code.\n   - **Top Bar Contract**: Follows the 3-zone standard (single-element brand wordmark, clean single-line navigation links, and primary kinetic `Request Audit` CTA).\n\n2. **Interactive Mobile Preview Stage (Live Device Simulator)**\n   - **Aetheria HFT Terminal**: Live simulated WebSocket orderbook depth, real-time price ticks, and instant buy/sell trade execution feedback.\n   - **BioPulse Continuous Telemetry**: Real-time continuous 120Hz Lead II ECG waveform, cardiac vitals (BPM, SpO2, HRV), and raw BLE packet hex streaming.\n   - **Vortex Gesture Physics**: Interactive draggable touch canvas powered by UI-thread spring calculations, displaying live coordinates and worklet latency.\n   - **Chronos Offline CRDT Ledger**: Interactive Online/Airplane mode toggle with direct SQLite C++ JSI commit simulation and vector clock conflict resolution.\n   - **Architecture Mode Comparator**: Live toggle between **New Architecture JSI (Zero-Copy C++)** and **Legacy Bridge (JSON-over-String)**, demonstrating frame rate degradation (dropping to ~36 FPS with Hermes GC pressure) vs. locked 120 FPS.\n\n3. **Systems & JSI Code Inspector**\n   - Terminal window styling with window dots, line numbers, and custom token highlighting.\n   - Interactive files: `AetheriaOrderBookHost.cpp`, `BioPulseShadowNode.mm`, `VortexFragmentShader.tsx`, and `ChronosVectorEngine.ts`.\n   - Click-to-inspect architectural invariants explaining zero-copy buffers, Yoga layout bypass, and Metal/Vulkan shader pipelines.\n   - Visual architectural pipeline mapping the thread distribution from the JS Thread (Hermes) through JSI C++ pointers into the Metal/Vulkan GPU surface.\n\n4. **Empirical Benchmarks & Dynamic Stress Tester**\n   - Interactive slider adjusting simulated WebSocket throughput (500 to 5,000 ticks/sec), dynamically calculating serialization lag, memory churn, and frame budget status.\n\n5. **Architecture Telemetry Log**\n   - Clean horizontal rows partitioned by structural hairlines with monospaced timestamps, Space Grotesk feature headlines, commit hashes, and `#65D6C5` performance gains (`+58 FPS`, `-32% TTI`, `-28MB Heap`). Filterable by subsystem.\n\n6. **Interactive Cockpit Terminal Console (`> adarsh.tech ~ $`)**\n   - Accessible via the top bar or by pressing the backtick/tilde key (`` ` ``).\n   - Executable commands: `neofetch`, `help`, `skills`, `projects`, `benchmarks`, `cat bio.md`, `audit`, and `clear`, with command history navigation.\n\n7. **Detailed Architecture Dossiers & Audit Request Flow**\n   - In-depth modal dossiers for case studies detailing challenges, architectural decisions, and outcomes.\n   - Systems review scheduling form generating verifiable reference IDs upon submission."
